    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">1D DP - string split</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/word-break/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 139</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Word Break</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">A prefix can be split exactly when some dictionary word ends it and the part before that word can be split: ok[i] = OR over j of (ok[j] and s[j..i) is a word). Only word lengths up to the longest word matter, so it is O(n·L²) time and O(n) extra space, where plain recursion is O(2^n).</p>\n"
